How dichotomous keys work
A dichotomous key is a series of paired statements (a couplet) where exactly one fits your specimen; each answer sends you to the next couplet until only one identity remains. Good couplets use observable, unambiguous features — number of legs, presence of wings, leaf shape — never vague words like 'big' or 'pretty'. Keys exist for plants, insects, fish, animal tracks and even bacteria (using staining and biochemical tests). Following a key trains the same skill doctors use in diagnosis and mechanics use in fault-finding: eliminate possibilities systematically instead of guessing.$wdthseed$, NULL, 30, 4, TRUE, TRUE, $wdthseed${"objectives":["Explain how a dichotomous key works","Use a key to identify unknown specimens","Construct a simple key for four specimens"],"introduction":"You find an insect you have never seen. Is it a pest, a pollinator, or harmless? A dichotomous key answers such questions with a chain of either-or choices.","key_points":["Couplets must be observable and mutually exclusive","Trace every step; never skip ahead","Unknown specimens stay unknown — never guess"],"references":["WOLI DAN TECH HUB original notes — identification keys worksheet (see assignment)"]}$wdthseed$::jsonb, (select id from public.course_modules where seed_key = $wdthseed$biology:mod01$wdthseed$), (select id from public.course_topics where seed_key = $wdthseed$biology:mod01:top02$wdthseed$), (select id from public.courses where slug = $wdthseed$biology$wdthseed$)) on conflict (seed_key) where seed_key is not null do update set title = excluded.title, description = excluded.description, lesson_type = excluded.lesson_type, video_url = excluded.video_url, content = excluded.content, resource_url = excluded.resource_url, duration = excluded.duration, order_number = excluded.order_number, is_published = excluded.is_published, published = excluded.published, metadata = excluded.metadata, module_id = excluded.module_id, topic_id = excluded.topic_id, course_id = excluded.course_id;
