From amino acids to proteins
Proteins contain C, H, O plus NITROGEN (and sometimes sulphur). Their monomers are 20 amino acids, joined by peptide bonds through condensation into polypeptides. Structure has four levels: PRIMARY — the exact amino-acid sequence (dictated by DNA; one wrong swap causes sickle-cell disease); SECONDARY — local folding into alpha-helices or beta-pleated sheets, held by hydrogen bonds; TERTIARY — the full 3D shape of one chain (this shape IS the function — an enzyme's active site, an antibody's binding site); QUATERNARY — several chains assembled (haemoglobin's four subunits). Heat, strong acids/alkalis and heavy metals disrupt the weak bonds, unfolding the protein — DENATURATION — which destroys function permanently. This is why a boiled egg never un-boils: its albumin proteins are denatured.

Protein jobs
Learn five roles with examples: (1) CATALYSIS — enzymes (amylase, catalase); (2) TRANSPORT — haemoglobin carries oxygen, membrane carriers move ions; (3) DEFENCE — antibodies tag germs, fibrinogen clots blood; (4) STRUCTURE — collagen in skin and bone, keratin in hair and nails, actin/myosin in muscle; (5) CONTROL — hormones such as insulin, and receptor proteins that receive signals. Kwashiorkor — the swollen-belly protein deficiency seen in malnourished children — shows what happens when the body cannot build these: stunted growth, weak immunity and fluid imbalance. Beans, soya, groundnuts, eggs, fish and milk are affordable complete-protein sources.$wdthseed$, NULL, 35, 3, TRUE, TRUE, $wdthseed${"objectives":["State that proteins are chains of amino acids joined by peptide bonds","Describe the four levels of protein structure simply","Give five roles of proteins with one example each"],"introduction":"Hair, enzymes, antibodies, haemoglobin and spider silk are all proteins — one construction kit producing endless machines. The secret is shape.","key_points":["Sequence → shape → function","Denaturation is usually irreversible","Kwashiorkor = protein deficiency disease"],"references":["OpenStax Biology 2e — Chapter 3 (proteins)"]}$wdthseed$::jsonb, (select id from public.course_modules where seed_key = $wdthseed$biology:mod03$wdthseed$), (select id from public.course_topics where seed_key = $wdthseed$biology:mod03:top02$wdthseed$), (select id from public.courses where slug = $wdthseed$biology$wdthseed$)) on conflict (seed_key) where seed_key is not null do update set title = excluded.title, description = excluded.description, lesson_type = excluded.lesson_type, video_url = excluded.video_url, content = excluded.content, resource_url = excluded.resource_url, duration = excluded.duration, order_number = excluded.order_number, is_published = excluded.is_published, published = excluded.published, metadata = excluded.metadata, module_id = excluded.module_id, topic_id = excluded.topic_id, course_id = excluded.course_id;
