Procedures and colours
STARCH — Iodine test: add yellow-brown iodine solution to the sample. Positive: BLUE-BLACK. Negative: stays brown-yellow. (No heating needed.) REDUCING SUGARS (glucose, maltose — NOT sucrose) — Benedict's test: add blue Benedict's solution, then heat in a water bath (never a bare flame). Positive: GREEN → YELLOW → ORANGE → BRICK-RED precipitate as sugar concentration rises. PROTEIN — Biuret test: add sodium hydroxide solution, then a few drops of dilute copper sulphate. Positive: PURPLE/VIOLET. Negative: stays blue. FATS — Emulsion test: shake the sample with ethanol, then pour into water. Positive: MILKY-WHITE EMULSION. (Alternative grease-spot: rub on paper — translucent spot that stays.) Non-reducing sugars (sucrose): boil first with dilute acid, neutralise, THEN Benedict's — a two-step test examiners love.

Safety and fair testing
Benedict's test needs heat: wear eye protection, use a water bath (no open flame near ethanol — it is flammable), point test tubes away from people, and use tongs. Biuret's sodium hydroxide is corrosive — rinse spills with plenty of water and report them. Fair-test rules: same sample size, same reagent volumes, same heating time, and a CONTROL (e.g. distilled water) to prove the reagents alone give negatives. Record results in a table with OBSERVATION (colour seen) and INFERENCE (nutrient present) as separate columns — mixing them loses marks.$wdthseed$, NULL, 35, 5, TRUE, TRUE, $wdthseed${"objectives":["State the reagent, method and positive result for each test","Explain the safety precautions for heating tests","Interpret combined results on unknown samples"],"introduction":"A white powder could be starch, sugar, protein or salt. Four colour-change tests identify it in minutes — and food-test questions are guaranteed marks if you memorise the colours.","key_points":["Colour triples: reagent + method + result","Sucrose is non-reducing — acid first","Observation and inference are separate columns"],"references":["OpenStax Biology 2e — Chapter 3 (macromolecule detection principles)"]}$wdthseed$::jsonb, (select id from public.course_modules where seed_key = $wdthseed$biology:mod03$wdthseed$), (select id from public.course_topics where seed_key = $wdthseed$biology:mod03:top03$wdthseed$), (select id from public.courses where slug = $wdthseed$biology$wdthseed$)) on conflict (seed_key) where seed_key is not null do update set title = excluded.title, description = excluded.description, lesson_type = excluded.lesson_type, video_url = excluded.video_url, content = excluded.content, resource_url = excluded.resource_url, duration = excluded.duration, order_number = excluded.order_number, is_published = excluded.is_published, published = excluded.published, metadata = excluded.metadata, module_id = excluded.module_id, topic_id = excluded.topic_id, course_id = excluded.course_i